{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "XGJz4Ibk9q", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-01", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919837, "segment_id": "TDISa12xaW", "segment_broadcast_id": "XGJz4Ibk9q", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Brian Williams (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919837, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "XGJz4Ibk9q", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-01", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919837, "segment_id": "ACiuEWkfDC", "segment_broadcast_id": "XGJz4Ibk9q", "segment_title": "Economy: Bailout Bill / Small Businesses", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.  \n\n(Capitol: Tom Costello) The vote in the Senate on a new financial rescue package featured; details given about new provisions and alternative plans; scenes shown of Senators John McCain and Barack Obama arriving in Washington, DC. [Senators Harry REID, Mitch McCONNELL\u2020\u2013 comment on getting the bill through the House.] [President BUSH \u2013 says it\u2019s very important for members to take this bill seriously.] [September 25, Senator Richard SHELBY\u2020- opposes the plan.] [Columbia University economics professor Joseph STIGLITZ\u2020- outlines things that should have been done.] [Representative Peter DeFAZIO\u2020- suggests trying an accounting change first.] [At an Obama rally in Florida, former President Bill CLINTON \u2013 says the Wall Street we knew is gone.]  \n\n(Studio: Brian Williams) The drop in auto sales for Ford, Chrysler and Toyota and showroom traffic cited.  \n\n(Studio: Brian Williams, Michelle Caruso-Cabrera) The impact of the credit crisis on car sales and Warren Buffett\u2019s investment in GE discussed  \n\n(Palm Bay, Florida: Roger O\u2019Neil) The effects of the economic crisis on city budgets examined; details given about service cuts and falling tax revenues; scenes shown from Palm Bay, Florida. [Palm Bay Mayor John MAZZIOTTI\u2020\u2020- says it\u2019s our job to make sure the worst is minimized.] [National League of Cities Chris HOENE\u2020- cites statistics on city finances.] [Palm Bay resident Carl WANNAMAKER\u2020- comments.] ", "segment_duration": 480, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919838, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "XGJz4Ibk9q", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-01", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919837, "segment_id": "3EW5yGYafB", "segment_broadcast_id": "XGJz4Ibk9q", "segment_title": "Decision 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / Vice Presidential Debate", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.   (Washington: Andrea Mitchell) Tomorrow\u2019s vice presidential debate between Senator Joe Biden and Governor Sarah Palin previewed; photo shown of Palin practicing at Senator John McCain\u2019s ranch; scenes shown of Biden greeting patrons at a diner, Palin not answering interviewer Katie Couric\u2019s question about magazines and newspapers and in a 2006 debate; details given of the challenges facing each. [At campaign rally, PALIN \u2013 jokes about Biden.] [September 10, BIDEN \u2013 says Senator Hillary Clinton is as qualified or more qualified to be vice president than he is.] [On \u201cThe Hugh Hewitt Show,\u201d voice of PALIN \u2013 says it\u2019s time that normal Joe Six-Pack American is represented in the vice presidency.] [On \u201cToday,\u201d former President George BUSH \u2013 notes Biden can\u2019t be seen as a chauvinist or bully.] [September 24, BIDEN \u2013 says he has no fear of debating a woman.] The challenge against moderator Gwen Ifill, who is writing a book about black politicians, noted. ", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63530.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919839, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "XGJz4Ibk9q", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-01", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919837, "segment_id": "wpnJxN6RMy", "segment_broadcast_id": "XGJz4Ibk9q", "segment_title": "Fossett Disappearance", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.  \n\n(Los Angeles: John Larson) The discovery in California of items belonging to adventurer Steve Fossett, who has been missing since September 2007, featured; scenes shown of the ID cards and money found by hiker Preston Morrow&#134;. [Voice of MORROW \u2013 comments.]  ", "segment_duration": 110, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63680.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919840, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "